WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.160
So, on Friday afternoon,
U.S. President Donald Trump

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:06.700
signed an Executive Order that
reshapes U.S. immigration law,

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.280
and there's been a lot of confusion
about it, even within the Government,

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.720
about who's affected by this law
and precisely what it means.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.340
So I thought today I'd take a closer look
at what the Executive Order actually says.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.720
So first, the order bans, for a period of 90 days,
all "immigrant and non immigrant"

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.720
entry into the United States
from all citizens of seven nations --

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.420
Iran, Iraq, Libya, Somalia, Sudan, and Yemen.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.980
These seven nations
seem to have been chosen

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.900
because they were cited
in 2015 and 2016 laws

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.180
signed by President Obama that
required residents of those countries

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.160
to get a visa to visit the United States.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.900
But the Executive Order states that they can't
enter the United States even with a visa,

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.080
although there are a few exceptions for diplomats.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.820
So what does this mean?
Well, for an Iranian professor at Yale,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.940
it means that if she leaves the U.S.
she won't be allowed to re-enter it,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.900
even though she's a well-known 
opponent of the Iranian regime.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.060
And for a doctor who is abroad 
battling a polio outbreak,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.660
it meant being denied entry into
the U.S. despite his visa to be here.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.260
Now, I know those probably sound like
particular examples of hard-luck stories,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.400
but because people from those
countries already needed visas

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.920
with specific reasons to
visit the United States,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.800
like visiting family, or studying,
or working in a specialized field,

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.700
almost all the stories are hard-luck stories.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.300
The Executive Order initially also seemed to apply
to legal, permanent residents of the United States

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.840
who aren't citizens -- so called "green card" holders,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.080
although the language in the order is extremely hard to
parse, like, even to those within the government.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.660
I mean, at one point on Sunday, Tump's chief of staff said the order "does not apply" to green card holders,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:39.100
and then later, in the very same interview, said
"of course it does" apply to green card holders.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.680
But after much confusion and emergency lawsuits,
it now appears that permanent residents

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.360
will not be subject to the ban.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.980
It's also unclear from the language in the order
whether it applies to dual citizens.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:52.720
Like, if you're a Canadian citizen who was born in
Somalia as Canada's Immigration Minister is,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.120
there's still some confusion as to 
whether you can enter the U.S.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.100
Now, critics of this part of the Executive Order,

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.800
and I should acknowledge that I am among them,

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.500
argue that it is really poorly targeted.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.400
I mean, no foreign nationals
from any of those seven countries

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.880
has killed even a single American
in a terrorist attack. Ever.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:14.840
In general, terrorism in the U.S. since 
9/11 has been exceedingly rare.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.860
Like, in the past decade, American civilians

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.280
are literally more likely to die
by lightning strike than terrorism.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.360
And notably, most of the attacks
that do happen in the U.S.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.320
are carried out by American
citizens or permanent residents,

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.000
and those attacks wouldn't be
prevented by the order.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.600
Now, the counterargument is that there may be threats
from these seven countries we don't know about,

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.460
but it's really hard to prove a negative,

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.360
like, it's hard for me to prove that I'm not a terrorist

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.340
because, how can you be sure I'm not?

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.200
Just for the record, in case
Big Brother is watching -- I'm not.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.900
"In case Big Brother..." de--
Big Brother is definitely watching.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.480
Anyway, all of this is why concerns about the ban
don't really fall along traditional left-right lines

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.380
like, the very conservative
Cato Institute, for instance, said

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.100
there is "little national security benefit to Trump's executive order on immigration."

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:00.000
And many, although by no means all,
Republican Congress people and Senators agree.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.220
John McCain and Lindsey Graham, for instance, released a statement saying that

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.400
the ban may be remembered as a self-inflicted wound in the fight against terrorism.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.880
And then there is the second part of the Executive Order,

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.340
which affects admission of refugees into the United States.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:18.300
So back in 2011, the Obama administration dramatically slowed the process of refugee applications

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.940
from Iraq for 6 months, an off-sided precedent for what Trump announced on Friday

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.800
but this is very different.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:30.500
Trump is suspending all refugee admission to the United States from all countries for 120 days,

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.840
and suspending all refugee resettlement from Syria indefinitely.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.700
This appears to include people who've already been vetted, approved and received visas,

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.320
which is also very different from what happened in 2011

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.440
Side-note -- you may have heard that there is no vetting of Syrian refugees coming into the United States,

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.260
that is simple not true.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.900
As discussed in this video, the process includes a huge variety of background checks and interviews,

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.580
and often takes more than two years.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.500
The Executive Order also prioritizes (quote)

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.260
"refugee claims made by individuals on the basis of religious-based persecution."

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.640
which Trump has said will mean prioritizing Christian refugees when the program restarts

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:10.800
although that's not actually stated in the order and it's not clear it would be legal.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.640
For context though, last year the US accepted about 39,000 Muslim refugees,

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.180
about 37,500 Christian ones, and also 8,500 people of other or no faith.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.200
But just to be absolutely clear, Muslim refugees who have been vetted and approved for admission

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:28.900
to the United States cannot currently get in, but neither can Christian or Buddhist refugees

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:34.240
for at leas 120 days, nor can interpreters who served with the American Armed Forces in Iraq,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.000
because no refugees are being allowed into the United States.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.200
And this blanket ban also seems to me very poorly targeted.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:46.520
For one thing, it lumps all refugees together, whether they're from Syria, or South Sudan, or Burma

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:51.820
Like, most refugees resettled in the United States in 2015 were not Syrian, they were Burmese.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:57.040
But also, many Syrian refugees are victims of ISIS who can speak first hand about its horrors

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.700
and that is a moderating force, not a radicalizing one.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:05.220
Imagining Syrians monolithically is as dangerously simplistic as imagining that

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:09.080
ending refugee resettlement will solve the US's security challenges.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:15.300
I share John McCain's feeling that ultimately this kind of blanket ban will do more to help terrorist recruitment

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.800
than improve our security.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.520
Now, Trump counters that it will make us more safe, and he certainly has access to top-secret information

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.960
that I don't have access to;

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:28.780
but given that these policies wouldn't've prevented a single US terror fatality from the last 40 years,

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.660
it's hard to see exactly how we're safer.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:35.860
There are also other issues of legal confusion in the order, for instance, the order states (quote)

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:40.300
"The United States cannot, and should not, admit those who do not support the Constitution."

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:44.300
But as many Law professors have pointed out -- that's kind of ludicrous.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.060
I mean, according to that sentence, if you are for instance, Canadian

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:51.960
and you support a parliamentary system of government over the system outlined in the US Constitution,

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:56.620
are you no longer legally allowed to visit Disney World? Because that does appear now to be the law.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:00.020
Also, when foreigners attempt to enter the United States, as in most countries,

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.560
they have the right to seek asylum, and be interviewed by an immigration officer

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.000
to determine if the asylum seeker has a credible fear of persecution

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.320
but the Executive Order explicitly states that "no benefits" will be extended

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.960
to citizens of the affected nations when they attempt to enter the United States

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.000
and such an interview would probably constitute a benefit.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.580
So as of now it does not appear that people are being allowed to seek asylum,

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:26.060
which is in violation of an existing US law, called the Immigration and Nationality Act,

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.900
which an Executive Order cannot legally override.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:33.220
In short, no matter how you feel about immigration, this Executive Order is a hot mess

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:37.200
it is too ambiguous, self contradictory, and unclear to be effective law.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.320
Now, I wanna emphasize that much of this may be moot in 3 or 4 months

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:41.800
as parts of the order expire,

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:45.860
but even if that occurs I worry we've already made a dangerous statement

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.540
that the US won't do its part in the refugee crisis,

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.100
and that we will discriminate based solely on place of birth.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.560
I think those are mistakes. That imagining a diverse group of over 100 million people

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:02.400
to be some terrifying and singular Other only encourages others to imagine us that way.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.300
It's hard to imagine people complexly, especially when you're being told to fear them,

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:12.500
but I found it helpful to listen, so I put together a playlist of refugees telling their stories

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:15.360
and ask you to listen to them, to believe them,

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.220
and to see them as people, instead of merely as threats.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:20.940
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

